# TakeOff, as the flight map menu's does it (takeOffToolStripMenuItem_Click): its box offers
# takeoff_alt - 5 the first time - the answer is saved, the vehicle is put in Guided and then told
# to take off. It does not arm; the pilot arms first. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:5404-5429`
#
# The owner's bug report of 2026-09-26, "unable to get simulation to takeoff": the button then sent
# the take-off alone, with no box and no Guided, and a copter armed in Stabilize refuses a take-off
# outside Guided. This arms in Stabilize, as he did, and takes off.
#
# THIS FLIES SITL: it arms, climbs and lands. Needs a copter SITL:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-takeoff.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 52
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions
click Stabilize
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize
expect vehicle.armed false
# SITL passes its pre-arm checks once its EKF and GPS are ready (hud-health.gui): a SITL just
# started refuses Arm until then, as a vehicle just powered does.
within 60
expect hud.prearm Ready to Arm
# And Guided, which TakeOff switches to, wants a position once armed: ArduCopter refuses it
# until its EKF has an absolute position from the GPS (position_ok) - disarmed, or in Stabilize,
# where the copter is armed, it asks for none. A SITL a few seconds old has not got one yet.
within 60
expect fly.ekf.flags ~ pos_horiz_abs On

# Armed in Stabilize, throttle down, as the owner armed it.
click arm
within 15
expect vehicle.armed true

# TakeOff's box, offering 5; 8 given.
click takeoff
expect fly.prompt Enter Takeoff Alt
expect fly.prompt.value 5
key ctrl+u
type 8
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
# setMode("GUIDED") first on the wire, then the take-off, which Guided lets the copter accept.
expect fly.sent ~ MAV_CMD_DO_SET_MODE
expect fly.sent ~ MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF 0,0,0,0,0,0,8
expect vehicle.mode Guided
within 10
expect fly.ack MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF: accepted
expect vehicle.armed true

# The box offers what was last given.
# Asked once a session (the owner's ruling, PLAN.md section 12 D24, 2026-10-03): the second
# TakeOff asks nothing and takes off at the height the first was given - which ArduCopter,
# already airborne, refuses ("can't takeoff again"); the C# would ask again.
expect fly.takeoff.remembered 8
expect fly.takeoff.sent 1
click takeoff
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.takeoff.sent 2
expect fly.sent ~ MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF 0,0,0,0,0,0,8

# Down again, and left in Stabilize, as the next test finds a fresh SITL: Land is not a mode a
# copter arms in, and a vehicle left there fails every later arming check.
click land
within 30
expect vehicle.armed false
click Stabilize
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize
